{# The memory-lifecycle section, shared by every engine template that feeds #}
{# the memory lifecycle findings. Parameterized by (findings list, heading #}
{# text, scan coverage record) so each template passes its own heading text #}
{# and the coverage the producing scan stamped. The body is #}
{# verbatim-pinned by the section suite in src/lib.rs — wording or formatting #}
{# drift fails CI. #}
{# The coverage record (issue #349) arrives as CoverageInfo strings: the #}
{# scan's status word and its admission line. The include appends exactly #}
{# one "Coverage:" qualification line — beside the entries, or as the whole #}
{# section beside the heading when the scan stamped no findings but admits #}
{# falling short — whenever the record carries an admission; a complete or #}
{# missing record renders exactly what it rendered before, and the line #}
{# names only bodies the scan never reached, never an examined-and-clean #}
{# body the finding list left unmentioned. #}
{% macro memory_lifecycle_section(findings, heading, coverage) %}
{% if !findings.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

The following memory lifecycles were recognized in this function by static
analysis. Where a finding is credible, express the resource with the suggested
Rust ownership pattern instead of transliterating the manual allocate/free or
open/close pairs:

{% for finding in findings %}
- **{{ finding.suggestion|safe }}** ({{ finding.kind }} lifecycle, confidence {{ finding.confidence }})
  Evidence: `{{ finding.evidence|safe }}`
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if !coverage.admission.is_empty() %}
{% if findings.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

{% endif %}
Coverage: {{ coverage.admission }}

{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
